 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "board is a non-empty rectangular 2D array of tiles; every tile is a two-character string whose first character is an uppercase letter (its terrain) and whose second is a digit 0-9 (its crowns). A region is a maximal group of tiles with the same terrain letter connected through horizontal or vertical neighbours. The score of a region is its number of tiles times the total crowns on its tiles. Return the sum of all region scores.",
